   1293  fe00							; LaserTipEnemy (2026-10-20) — enemy covering the beam's TIP PIXEL, tested
   1294  fe00							; BEFORE the wall clamp. The clamp only looks at the tip CELL, so an enemy
   1295  fe00							; drawn over a solid cell (the snake's whole design: it retreats into its
   1296  fe00							; wall) lost to the wall and a visible hit did nothing (user report). A
   1297  fe00							; sprite overlaps the tip pixel iff eX-7 <= tip <= eX, i.e. eX in
   1298  fe00							; [tip, tip+7] — an enemy BEHIND the wall cannot match, because the tip px
   1299  fe00							; sits inside the solid cell and the next sprite starts past it. Also covers
   1300  fe00							; the air-tip case harmlessly (same kill the body loop would award).
   1301  fe00							; IN: CollisionX = tip arg (LaserX, unchanged), PlayerDir = facing.
   1302  fe00							; OUT: A=0 no tip enemy -> LaserWallClamp (normal wall/enemy order);
   1303  fe00							;	A=$50 kill / A=1 lamp -> ReturnPad (caller resets the beam).
